==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pitch out}}

# {{lb|en|baseball}} A pitch which was [[intentionally]] [[thrown]] [[outside]] to the catcher who stands up with the pitch for the purpose of [[enabling]] the [[catcher]] to [[throw out]] a [[runner]].
#: ''The '''pitch out''' enabled the catcher to throw out the runner.''

===Verb===
{{en-verb|pitches out|pitching out|pitched out}}

# {{lb|en|baseball|intransitive}} To intentionally throw the ball outside to the catcher who stands up with the pitch for the purpose of enabling the catcher to throw out a runner
#: ''Jones '''pitched out''' twice to no avail.''

